8% error rate. You confirmed payments-worker was the cause and the API errors were a knock-on effect.\n2. **Rollback:** v3.3.0 is the last payments-worker release that was healthy in production. It's now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%, and the service reports healthy.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 is a SEV2 for payments-worker. The first attempt to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list, found nothing there, and tried again. There's only one incident, so on-call was paged once.\n\n**Still open:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0, marked unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. If it doesn't, the API may have its own problem. Its last healthy release was v5.0.0. I haven't rolled it back because you said the worker was the cause. If the errors continue, I can roll it back to v5.0.0 if you want.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PcF9JFDmk18dFkCNfCH8Fg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014fg1eYFwHM55oWKAykrGoM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013a5mMNUcRFtdFie434y3BF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011JawhMMgS97cbxZ8uQPizj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QqhmPJ6PSoJWemX7WPea7G", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018dGkJBNVRvT2Gy